{"id":"e02t2","name":"Pallet Label Grid","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","rows_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Pallets in a warehouse carry a printed label grid. Product words are printed <b>vertically</b>: each word is written from top to bottom inside one column of the grid. A column can hold several words, separated by one or more <code>#</code> characters, and <code>#</code> is also used to fill empty cells. A camera scans the grid row by row.</p>\n<p>You are given <code>rows_df</code> with the columns <code>row_no</code> (integer, <code>1</code> is the top row) and <code>text</code> (string). Rows can have <b>different lengths</b>: a row that is shorter than the others has no character in the last columns, which is the same as <code>#</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to extract every word of the grid:</p>\n<ol><li>columns are numbered from left to right, starting at <code>1</code>;</li><li>read the characters of a column from the top row to the bottom row; the words of the column are the non-empty pieces between <code>#</code> characters;</li><li>words of a column are numbered from top to bottom, starting at <code>1</code>.</li></ol>\n<p>Return <code>col_no</code>, <code>word_no</code> and <code>word</code>, sorted by <code>col_no</code>, then <code>word_no</code>. The rows of <code>rows_df</code> are not given in any particular order.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>rows_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>row_no</th><th>text</th></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>L</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>#IWI</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>E#R</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>TS</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>II</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>AKOF</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>OW#G</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>col_no</th><th>word_no</th><th>word</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>TEA</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>OIL</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>S</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>KIWI</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>ROW</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>FIG</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>Column <code>1</code> reads <code>\"TEA#OIL\"</code> from top to bottom, so it holds two words. Row <code>1</code> is <code>\"TS\"</code>: it is too short to reach columns <code>3</code> and <code>4</code>, so these cells count as <code>#</code>.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, rows_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return rows_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["grille","posexplode","collect_list ordonné","split regex"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"rows_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"row_no INT, text STRING","rows":[[7,"L"],[4,"#IWI"],[2,"E#R"],[1,"TS"],[6,"II"],[3,"AKOF"],[5,"OW#G"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["col_no","word_no","word"],"rows":[[1,1,"TEA"],[1,2,"OIL"],[2,1,"S"],[2,2,"KIWI"],[3,1,"ROW"],[4,1,"FIG"]]}},{"input":{"rows_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"row_no INT, text STRING","rows":[[1,"#A"],[2,"#BC"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["col_no","word_no","word"],"rows":[[2,1,"AB"],[3,1,"C"]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}